sts the SQL authors with no shares and no ranking, and says Ravi is the only author of database_sql.go. It tells the user to ask Ravi.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"No share of lines owned by departed people. It says Borman may still be involved, and it treats Rowe's identities as unconfirmed.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Lists Sam Okafor as a recent maintainer of time.go. It does not credit Noor Haddad with 0 lines, and it says only that Kofi's date is bad.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Names Paul Borman as main author of time.go with 73.0% (111 lines) and says he has left the project. Okafor holds none of the lines. His stated last commit year is off, but the substance matches.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"MikeWang has 81.2% of version7.go. Mei Chen has 9.4% and wrote the Time7 accessor, which Ravi committed. Ravi has only 1.9%.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Follows the rename to database_sql.go. Justin Overfelt has 39.6% of database_sql.go alone, which is in range, though the headline figure is a combined 60.5%. Stone, Wheeler and Souza are named, and all are gone.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Gives the departed share of lines as about 95.7% (4.3% active). It calls Mei Chen active and recommends her first for version7.go. It does not clearly name Ravi, Rowe and Kofi as the only active people.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Okafor's whitespace commit is explained and Okafor holds no lines. No generated files are counted and no bot is treated as a person. Noor and Kofi are not mentioned, but nothing in the answer contradicts the criterion.\",\"pass\":true}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"The final answer is only a note about a background-command notification. It says nothing about time.go.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Nothing about version7.go.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Nothing about the SQL code.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Nothing about who is still active.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"No content addresses the noise cases.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Credits Sam Okafor with 100% of time.go from raw blame and does not name Borman as the main author.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"MikeWang has about 86%, Mei Chen has 11 lines, and Ravi has 2 lines. Ravi is not credited with Mei's lines.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Follows the rename to database_sql.go. Overfelt has 26 lines (about 44% of the file), followed by Stone 11, Wheeler 8 and Souza 8. All are gone, and Ravi did only the rename.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Gives no repo-wide share of lines owned by departed people. It lists Mei Chen and Sam Okafor as possible reviewers, and it leaves Rowe's identities unconfirmed.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Names Sam Okafor as the owner of all of time.go and lists them as a person to ask. That is the noise the criterion says to exclude.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":12415,"type":"result","duration_ms":24726,"uuid":"8683ac18-855f-45ba-9ead-8137f7b383b7","ttft_stream_ms":1771,"time_to_request_ms":416,"first_content_frame_ms":1771,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
